-|\n","| 8 | 38.95 ± 0.09 ms |\n","| 16 | 10.95 ± 0.17 ms |\n","| 32 | 11.27 ± 0.14 ms |\n","\n","**Discussion:**\n","Smaller patch sizes (e.g., 8x8) preserve much more spatial detail but drastically increase the sequence length, leading to much higher computational costs (as seen in the ~39ms time). We would accept this trade-off in tasks requiring fine-grained visual understanding, such as small object detection, OCR, or dense segmentation, where high spatial resolution is strictly necessary for accuracy.\n","\n","#### 3. Symmetric InfoNCE Curves\n","**Plots:** *(Insert plots or links here)*\n","\n","**Discussion:**\n","The training loss curve demonstrates a steady decrease over the 10 epochs, indicating that the model successfully learned to align the image and text representations in the shared embedding space. Correspondingly, the zero-shot validation accuracy curve shows a strong upward trend, ultimately reaching a final accuracy of 84.16%. This inverse relationship highlights the effectiveness of the symmetric InfoNCE loss in optimizing for cross-modal zero-shot classification without overfitting.\n","\n","#### 4. Mask Diagrams & Validation Accuracies\n","**Diagrams:** *(Insert images here)*\n","\n","**Table:**\n","| Setup | Validation Accuracy |\n","|---|---|\n","| Setup A | |\n","| Setup B | |\n","\n","**Discussion:**\n","\n","#### 5. Freezing Strategies\n","**Table:** *(4 rows)*\n","\n","**Discussion:**"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"f9c8534a"},"source":["#### 6. Qualitative Evaluation\n","**Examples Table:** *(10 rows)*\n","\n","**Discussion:**\n","\n","#### 7. RoPE Extrapolation\n","**Table:**\n","| PE Method | Train-size Acc | Extrapolated-size Acc |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| Method 1 | |\n","| Method 2 | |\n","\n","**Discussion:**\n","\n","#### 8. M-RoPE Subquestions\n","**Answer 1:**\n","\n","**Answer 2:**\n","\n","**Answer 3:**\n","\n","#### 9. Spatial Relations\n","**Table:**\n","| Metric | Accuracy |\n","|---|---|\n","| Overall | |\n","| Spatial | |\n","\n","**Discussion:**\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"3b0cb7d5","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780003069201,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":6020,"user":{"displayName":"Hon Kit Jason Siu","userId":"06063984132850885963"}},"outputId":"515a21f4-a1cf-41b9-efdf-2b4512a8f488"},"source":["import torch\n","import torch.nn.functional as F\n","\n","def clip_loss(image_embeds: torch.Tensor, text_embeds: torch.Tensor, temperature: float = 1.0) -> torch.Tensor:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Computes the symmetric InfoNCE loss for CLIP.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        image_embeds: (B, d) L2-normalized image embeddings\n","        text_embeds: (B, d) L2-normalized text embeddings\n","        temperature: float to scale logits\n","    \"\"\"\n","    # 1. Compute similarity matrix (logits)\n","    # Since inputs are L2-normalized, dot product is cosine similarity.\n","    # Scale by temperature.\n","    logits = (image_embeds @ text_embeds.T) / temperature\n","\n","    # 2. Create labels\n","    # The positive pairs are on the diagonal (i-th image matches i-th text)\n","    B = image_embeds.size(0)\n","    labels = torch.arange(B, device=image_embeds.device)\n","\n","    # 3. Compute cross entropy loss in both directions\n","    # Image-to-text loss (rows)\n","    loss_i2t = F.cross_entropy(logits, labels)\n","\n","    # Text-to-image loss (columns)\n","    loss_t2i = F.cross_entropy(logits.T, labels)\n","\n","    # 4. Symmetric InfoNCE loss is the average of both\n","    loss = (loss_i2t + loss_t2i) / 2.0\n","\n","    return loss\n","\n","# --- Quick Test --- #\n","if __name__ == '__main__':\n","    B = 4\n","    d = 128\n","    # Create random embeddings and L2 normalize them\n","    dummy_img = F.normalize(torch.randn(B, d), p=2, dim=1)\n","    dummy_txt = F.normalize(torch.randn(B, d), p=2, dim=1)\n","\n","    loss_val = clip_loss(dummy_img, dummy_txt, temperature=0.07)\n","    print(f\"Calculated Symmetric InfoNCE Loss: {loss_val.item():.4f}\")"],"execution_count":10,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Calculated Symmetric InfoNCE Loss: 2.0432\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1e038f59"},"source":["### Pretraining CLIP\n","Run this cell to start training and generate the curves required for the written deliverable."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"03c8e6db","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1780003139627,"user_tz":420,"elapsed":70406,"user":{"displayName":"Hon Kit Jason Siu","userId":"06063984132850885963"}},"outputId":"d1e1b9f1-e9cb-4e0b-fcc4-026651f6de75"},"source":["%cd /content/drive/MyDrive/hw3\n","!uv run python scripts/pretrain_clip.py --config configs/clip_eurosat.yaml\n"],"execution_count":11,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["/content/drive/MyDrive/hw3\n","\u001b[2K\u001b[2mUninstalled \u001b[1m1 package\u001b[0m \u001b[2min 16ms\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[2K░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ [0/1] \u001b[2mInstalling wheels...                                 \u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[33mwarning\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m \u001b[1mFailed to hardlink files; falling back to full copy. This may lead to degraded performance.\n","         If the cache and target directories are on different filesystems, hardlinking may not be supported.\n","         If this is intentional, set `export UV_LINK_MODE=copy` or use `--link-mode=copy` to suppress this warning.\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[2K\u001b[2mInstalled \u001b[1m1 package\u001b[0m \u001b[2min 144ms\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","Traceback (most recent call last):\n","  File \"/content/drive/MyDrive/hw3/scripts/pretrain_clip.py\", line 15, in <module>\n","    from torch.utils.tensorboard import SummaryWriter\n","  File \"/content/drive/MyDrive/hw3/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/torch/utils/tensorboard/__init__.py\", line 1, in <module>\n","    import tensorboard\n","ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 